  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational design of therapeutic proteins using generative and learning-based models that operate over sequence and structure. Pythia-1 is an all-atom generative model over sequence and 3D structure that designs full-length IgG antibodies for 22 targets, including GPCR agonists and antagonists. AbOptimizer applies reinforcement learning to multiproperty antibody optimization through parallel multisite sequence editing. LPT orchestrates bounded LLM agent loops, supported by a curated database of about 14000 papers, for de novo protein binder design. What is new is multiproperty optimization and agentic orchestration layered onto structure-aware generation. A cell-free synthesis study that generates scRNA-seq profiles of immune responses to designed signals sits adjacent to this thread, linking computational design to experimental readout of intercellular signaling.",
